  1729	# ---- 5c-bis-3 framework version marker (PLAN-166 F3 / ADR-155-AMEND-1) ----
  1730	# .claude/.framework-version is a TRACKED file of the framework repo (one
  1731	# line, byte-identical to VERSION — the bump writes it as its 12th site and
  1732	# verify-counts.sh cross-checks it every release). It is the forensic anchor
  1733	# that stays true POST-UPGRADE: upgrade.sh deliberately never touches the
  1734	# root VERSION (S238/ADR-155 class), so on an upgraded adopter only this
  1735	# marker reports the installed framework version. It lives inside .claude/,
  1736	# so it is delivered in BOTH ceremonies (the WS4 user-ceremony guard only
  1737	# forbids root files). The write is EXPLICIT — the manifest enumeration
  1738	# never delivers anything, it only records (r7) — and skip-if-exists: a
  1739	# pre-existing marker stays adopter-owned (no delivery record), and every
  1740	# marker-first reader keyed off that record falls back to VERSION (r20).
  1741	install_framework_marker() {
  1742	  if [[ ! -f "$SOURCE_DIR/.claude/.framework-version" ]]; then
